    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`). The audit output confirms the new behaviour end-to-end:\n\n```\nAUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"V2NSW2616E6609E9\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\",\"schemaVersion\":2}\n```\n\nHere's what I changed to release version 2 of the owner identity:\n\n**Version-2 identity derivation** (`OwnerRestControllerV1`)\n- `identityRegionCode` now prefixes the plain region with a fixed `V2` tag \u2192 e.g. `V2NSW`, so it flows into the `memberId` (`V2NSW2616E6609E9`) and every member id lands in a disjoint space from any v1 value.\n- `householdId` mixes `V2|` into its SHA-256 input.\n- `identityKey` mixes `V2|` into its SHA-256 input (kept as the single source used by both the duplicate check and the response).\n\nThe shared tag lives in one place: `OwnerMapper.IDENTITY_VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"`.\n\n**User-facing fields stay plain** (`OwnerMapper`)\n- `regionPrefix` reads the region back by matching `V2`+region name and returns the *plain* code, so `locality` stays `NSW`, `timezone` stays `Australia/Sydney`, and the owner segment's region stays plain \u2014 the `V2` tag never leaks out.\n- `memberIdFiscalYearSegment` skips the tag length so `fiscalYear` (`FY26`) is still read correctly from the v2 id.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` \u2192 generated DTOs)\n- New `OwnerIdentity` schema groups `memberId`, `householdId`, `identityKey`.\n- `Owner` drops those three top-level properties, gains a nested `identity` object and a top-level integer `apiVersion` (=2). The controller builds the `identity` object and sets `apiVersion`; the owner segment is recomputed from the v2 identity via `locality`.\n\n**Audit schema** (`OwnerCreatedEvent`)\n- Added `schemaVersion` (=2) to the structured event.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. The shipped acceptance test (which asserts `apiVersion==2`, the nested `identity.*` fields, and absence of the old top-level identifiers) passes.",
