    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered list of everything that fires when you `POST /api/owners`. The handler is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:186`), which delegates to the private `createOwner` (line 225).\n\n## Before the controller body runs\n\n1. **Bean Validation of `OwnerFieldsDto`** \u2014 triggered by `@Valid @RequestBody` on the generated `OwnersApi` interface. In field order: `firstName` (`@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size 1\u201330`), `lastName` (`@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size 1\u201330`), `address`/`addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (`@Size 1\u2013255` each, optional), `city` (`@NotNull`, `@Size 1\u201380`), `postcode` (`@Pattern ^[0-9]{4}$`, optional), `telephone` (`@NotNull`, `@Size 1\u201330`), `email` (`@Size 1\u2013255`, `@Email`, optional). *(The `Owner` entity's own annotations are NOT re-checked on this path.)*\n2. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`.\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header; if already recorded, returns the existing owner with **200 OK** and skips everything below.\n\n## Inside `createOwner` \u2014 validations & normalizations (nothing persisted yet)\n\n4. **`normalizeAddress`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 mutates the DTO: trims/collapses/upper-cases/expands address lines and recomposes the flat `address`.\n5. **`rejectBlankOwnerFields`** *(validation)* \u2014 400 if firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone are whitespace-only.\n6. **`rejectDisposableEmailDomain`** *(validation)* \u2014 400 if the email domain is blocklisted (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail).\n7. Reads the `sharesHousehold` flag (used later at step 17).\n8. **`rejectInvalidPostcode`** *(validation)* \u2014 400 if a present postcode is out of range for the city's region (NSW/VIC/QLD bands).\n9. **`rejectCityAtCapacity`** *(validation)* \u2014 409 if the city already has \u2265 50 owners.\n10. **`rejectFutureRegistrationDate`** *(validation)* \u2014 400 if the supplied registration date is after today (checked on the raw value).\n11. **Compute registration date** \u2014 supplied value (else today), then `businessDay(...)` rolls weekends/holidays forward.\n12. **`rejectDailyRegistrationLimit`** *(validation)* \u2014 429 if \u2265 100 owners already carry that adjusted date.\n13. **Normalize telephone** *(side-effect)* \u2014 to E.164, written back onto the DTO.\n14. **Normalize email** *(side-effect)* \u2014 lower-cased, written back onto the DTO.\n\n## Build entity + derived fields\n\n15. **`ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)`** \u2014 MapStruct map (id/pets ignored); set business-day registration date.\n16. **Derive `memberId`** (region+FY+hash+Luhn check, de-duped), **`namesakeCount`**, **`householdId`** (SHA-256 of lastName+postcode, null if no postcode).\n17. **`rejectDuplicateIdentity`** *(validation)* \u2014 409 if an existing non-deleted owner has the same identity key (SHA-256 of telephone+email+Soundex(lastName)). This is the single hard duplicate check.\n18. **`setPossibleDuplicateOf`** \u2014 soft duplicate hint: null if `sharesHousehold`, else first owner with same postcode + last-name Soundex but different identity.\n\n## Persist and post-save side-effects (order-critical)\n\n19. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` \u2014 the commit point; DB id assigned. (`CallMonitoringAspect` wraps this repository call for JMX metrics.)\n20. **`setHouseholdSize`** \u2014 computed *after* save so the owner counts itself (transient field).\n21. **`auditOwnerCreated`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 writes a human-readable AUDIT log line, then emits an `OwnerCreatedEvent` (JSON, monotonic per-JVM sequence) to the AUDIT logger. *(Plain logging \u2014 not published via `ApplicationEventPublisher`; no `@EventListener` consumes it.)*\n22. **`enqueueWelcomeNotification`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 one line on the NOTIFY logger.\n\n## Back in `addOwner`\n\n23. **`idempotencyKeyStore.record(key, owner.getId())`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 so a repeat returns the same owner.\n24. **Build response** \u2014 `OwnerDto` with recomputed derived fields, `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, **201 CREATED**.\n\n**Notable ordering facts:** all validation precedes the save at step 19; `householdSize` is deliberately computed *after* save; audit fires before notify; and `addOwner` is **not** `@Transactional`, so the log-based audit/notify side-effects are not bound to a transaction commit. There are **no** `@PrePersist`/`@PreUpdate` lifecycle callbacks and **no** Spring event listeners in this flow."
